<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Arras (1435)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1435</span> · Also known as Congress of Arras · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Arras of 21 September 1435 reconciled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france">Charles VII of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, ending the Burgundian alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. Philip recognised Charles as king in return for the towns of the Somme and a personal exemption from homage. Without Burgundian support the English position in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> weakened, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> fell to Charles in 1436.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-arras-1435.jpg" alt="Treaty of Arras (1435)" width="320" height="343" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ais_5054,_fol._86_recto,_Conf%C3%A9rences_d%27Arras_(1435).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
